 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to providing for the financing and construction of capital facilities for Broad Channel Volunteer Fire Department and Ambulance Corps, a not-for-profit corporation",
    "basePrintNo": "S7140",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7140-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1676 & 1680, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7140\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to providing\nfor the financing and construction of capital facilities for Broad\nChannel Volunteer Fire Department and Ambulance Corps, a\nnot-for-profit corporation\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nThis legislation will allow funding that has been allocated from the\nUnited States Department of Transportation to the Broad Channel\nVolunteer Fire Department and Ambulance Corps Inc., to be channeled\nthrough the New York State Dormitory Authority.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection 1. Paragraph (b) of subdivision 2 of section 1676 of the\npublic authorities law is amended by adding a new undesignated\nparagraph to read as follows:\n\nBroad Channel Volunteer Fire Department and Ambulance Corps, Inc. for\nthe purpose of providing construction related services in connection\nwith the construction, reconstruction, improvement, renovation,\ndevelopment or expansion of facilities owned by Broad Channel\nVolunteer Fire Department and Ambulance Corps, Inc. located at 23 West\n11th Road, Broad Channel, New York.\n\nSection 2. Subdivision 1 of section 1680 of the public authorities law\nis amended by adding a new undesignated paragraph to read as follows:\n\nBroad Channel Volunteer Fire Department and Ambulance Corps, Inc. for\nthe purpose of providing construction related services in connection\nwith the construction, reconstruction, improvement, renovation,\ndevelopment or expansion of facilities owned by Broad Channel\nVolunteer Fire Department and Ambulance Corps, Inc. located at 23 West\n11th Road, Broad Channel, New York.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe U.S. Department of Transportation previously allocated $2 million\nto the Broad Channel Volunteer Fire Department and Ambulance Corps,\nInc. for construction of a firehouse. At the recommendation of the New\nYork State Department of Transportation, this legislation will allow\nfor the funding to be channeled through the New York State Dormitory\nAuthority so that the funds may be accessed by the Broad Channel\nVolunteer Fire Department and Ambulance Corps, Inc. and will allow for\ngreater oversight by the Dormitory Authority.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThe bill would take effect immediately.\n",
